ggml-webgpu: Adreno SOFT_MAX / row-reduction / mat-vec defaults from the phone perf sweep.

POCO F5 Pro (Adreno 740), PLaMo 3 0.8B, round-3 per-op run: SOFT_MAX took 38% of decode and
75% of prompt time, the fused RMS_NORM+MUL 13% of decode. Both are one workgroup per row with
maxComputeInvocationsPerWorkgroup (1024 on Adreno) threads, for rows of 128-2048 values, and
SOFT_MAX also keeps a dynamically indexed private array (scratch memory on Adreno).

On Adreno:
- SOFT_MAX uses a variant without the private cache (NO_CACHE): the same three passes, values
  recomputed from src, shared-memory tree reductions in uniform control flow, no subgroups;
- SOFT_MAX and the fused RMS_NORM+MUL use 256-wide workgroups;
- the workgroup-reduction mat-vec uses 64-wide workgroups (phone: 2.92 -> 3.47 tok/s).
The fused RMS_NORM+MUL squares with v * v instead of pow(v, 2.0) (pow is undefined for
negative bases in WGSL) on every GPU. Other GPUs keep their shaders and sizes.

Tokens (after the profile name): rwg64|rwg128|rwg256|rwg512|rwg1024 row-reduction width,
smnc / smup new / upstream SOFT_MAX, and mvwg256 for the previous mat-vec width. Per-op timing
(perfops) also reports the SOFT_MAX row length and row count.

